<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/60008%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Prinas (river)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/59822%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/59852%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Pliny the Elder describes the ancient Prinas River as a navigable river that debouches into the Ganges. The Barrington Atlas Map-by-Map Directory indicates that the Prinas corresponds to the modern Tons River. The Tons is a modern-day tributary of the Yamuna River (the ancient Iomanes/Iobares), itself the second-largest tributary of the Ganges.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/60008> .

