<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/612196406%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Coombe Crag Roman Quarry";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/91358%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Evidence of Roman quarrying activity was discovered at Coombe Crag, a site some 350 meters south of the line of Hadrian's Wall. The quarry was used as a source of building materials for the Wall and at least eight inscriptions were identified on the sandstone cliff.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/612196406> .

