<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/621165832%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Pythionike monument";
    rdfs:comment "A cenotaph monument in western Attica praised by Pausanias, the Pythionike monument was located along the Sacred Way linking Athens and Eleusis. Stewart (2012) speculates whether Sulla could have plundered statuary from the monument when he marched on Athens.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/621165832> .

