<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/621925238%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Assur Archive 26";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/536694247%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893945%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Southwest of the Adad ziqqurrat in Assur, in dE5V, researchers found 6 clay tablets, some of which had envelopes, in the remains of a destroyed private house. The archive, belonging to Dadaya, dates to the reigns of Aššur-etel-ilāni (ca. 630–627 BC) and Sin-šarru-iškun (ca. 626-612 BC) and mostly contains loan documents.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/621925238> .

