<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/62810657/siqqurrat-ninurta> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jnovotny>;
    dcterms:description "The Sumerian (or Akkadian) ceremonial name of the ziggurat at Kalhu is not recorded in extant Assyrian texts. An Akkadian text of the ninth-century-BC Assyrian king Shalmaneser III (r. 858–824 BC) inscribed on two bricks discovered at Kalhu refer to the temple-tower as the “ziggurat of the god Ninurta.”";
    dcterms:modified "2024-08-15T16:25:46-04:00";
    dcterms:subject "ANE",
        "Assyrian";
    dcterms:title "siqqurrat Ninurta";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/62810657/siqqurrat-ninurta> .

