    rdfs:label "Graecostadium";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/337325364%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Located in Regio VIII of the ancient city of Rome, Graecostadium refers to a place that is either an area that is enclosed by walls or a set of buildings. This seems to have been a large area in any case. The Graecostadium is damaged by fire and subsequently restored under Antoninus Pius. Ths place burned again during the reign of Carinus.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/630721026> .

