<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/630799745%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "London Wall";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79574%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "London's original Roman wall in stone was built ca. A.D. 190 to 225. The wall originally had a length of ca. 4 km (2.5 miles and enclosed an area of ca. 134 hectares. It once included four city gates.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/630799745> .

