<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Saintes-Marie-de-la-Mer Roman Port";
    rdfs:comment "A Roman commercial port near the modern French town of Saintes-Maries-de-la-Mer is attested by over forty Roman-era shipwrecks discovered in the area since the 1990s, most carrying cargoes of metal. The excavators posit in Roman times a significantly different coastline (generally further south) and an old mouth of the Rhone (Ancien Rhône de Saint-Ferréol), located to the east of Saintes-Maries-de-la-Mer (Long 2011, Figure 1).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472/imagery-location-approximate-centerpoint-of-wreck-scatter> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:description "After Gosselin 2023, Figure 1 and Long 2011, Figure 1.";
    dcterms:modified "2023-08-16T22:22:36-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Imagery Location: Approximate Centerpoint of Wreck Scatter";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472/imagery-location-approximate-centerpoint-of-wreck-scatter> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472/imagery-location-grau-de-la-fourcade-saintes-maries-de-la-mer> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:description "The Grau de la Fourcade is the sea channel now occupying the point where the old Saint-Ferréol branch of the Rhone once debouched into the sea, a feature thought by the excavators to have been in place in Roman times.";
    dcterms:modified "2023-08-16T22:22:36-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Imagery Location: Grau de la Fourcade / Saintes-Maries-de-la-Mer";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472/imagery-location-grau-de-la-fourcade-saintes-maries-de-la-mer> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472/osm-location-of-modern-saintes-maries-de-la-mer> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
