<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/632219266%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Cento Camerelle (Bacoli)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432941%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called Cento Camerelle at Bacoli is an archaeological site that dates initially to the late republican period. A multi-story structure with provisions for a water system and cisterns, the building is linked initially to the Roman consul Quintus Hortensius Hortalus and later to Antonia Minor, the mother of the emperor Claudius.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/632219266> .

