<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/632604713%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Tell Djassa";
    rdfs:comment "Tell Djassa is an archaeological site in the upper Khabur River basin identified by salvage excavations in 1988-1990. Four main phases of human occupation were identified, all belonging to the third millennium BCE. The site was re-settled in the later first millennium BCE as demonstrated by Hellenistic pottery.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/632604713> .

