<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/638871%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Isinda (Lycian)";
    rdfs:comment "Ruins of the walled acropolis of ancient Isinda in Lycia are variously said by modern scholars to be located either \"above\" or 2-3km south of the modern Turkish village of Belenli, which is in Antalya province. BAtlas and OpenStreetMap generally agree (within their accuracy and precision limits) with the location further south.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/638871> .

