<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/638922%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Kissidai? Pr.";
    rdfs:comment "An ancient place, mentioned in the so-called Stadiasmus Maris Magni, that was probably a promontory (cape) and can likely be identified with the modern İblis Burnu (Cape İblis/Cape Angistro on the Turkish coast of the Gulf of Fethiye).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/638922> .

