<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/639153005%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Step Gate";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874621%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/882947620%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/945930916%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Most 7th-century B.C. Assyrian inscriptions record that Nineveh had eight south- and east-facing gates: the Step Gate was the sixth of these. The Neo-Assyrian king Sennacherib constructed it and gave it the Akkadian ceremonial name Mušēṣât-šīr-asakki, which means \"The One Who Exorcises the 'Flesh' of the Asakku-demon.\"";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/639153005> .

