<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648012835%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Olevano Romano";
    rdfs:comment "Remains of polygonal masonry fortification are extant at Olevano Romano in Italy, which is presumed to be the site of a fortified oppidum of the Aequi. The modern comune of Olevano Romano is located in Lazio, about 45 km to the east of Rome. Pre-Roman polygonal masonry walls underlie medieval architecture in the centro storico.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648012835> .

