<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/658450%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Daphne";
    rdfs:comment "Described by Strabo as a village (katoikia) about 40 stadia (~6 km) outside Antioch, Daphne today is known as Harbiye, in Turkey's Hatay province. In ancient times, it was home to a sacred grove and sanctuary of Apollo and Artemis, but today there are no visible monumental structures of ancient date.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/658450> .

