        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433014%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/433101%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/812127750%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Aqua Augusta (Naples), also known as the Acquedotto romano del Serino, is a complex aqueduct system supplying Roman-period sites in the Bay of Naples. The aqueduct system was built between ca. 33 and 12 B.C. It supplied a number of Campanian centers, including Pompeii, Herculaneum, and Puteoli.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/662332233> .

