<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/663286875%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ekišnugal";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/570809828%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912985%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The temple of the moon god Nanna/Suen/Sîn at Ur from the third to first millennium B.C. Over the course of its long history, it was rebuilt (and expanded) numerous times. A few of its more famous builders were Narām-Sîn of Agade, Ur-Nammu of Ur, and Nebuchadnezzar II of Babylon.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/663286875> .

