<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/663740691%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Isola de San Lazzaro degli Armeni";
    rdfs:comment "Small island in the Venetian Lagoon. A church and monastery were constructed on the site during the 9th century CE, and it was used as a leper colony in the medieval and early modern periods. Since 1717 CE, it has been home to an Armenian Catholic (Mkhitarist) monastery, from which the island derives its modern name.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/663740691> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/663740691/isola-san-lazzaro-degli-armeni> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/gmckee>;
    dcterms:description "Polygon representing the modern extent of the Isola di San Lazzaro degli Armeni, derived from an OpenStreetMap Way.";
    dcterms:modified "2026-05-07T12:22:07-04:00";
    dcterms:title "OSM location of Isola San Lazzaro degli Armeni";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/663740691/isola-san-lazzaro-degli-armeni> .

