<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/666765291%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Temple of Hadrian";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422863%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/936873471%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Temple of Hadrian at Rome, also referred to as the Hadrianeum, was a temple located in the Campus Martius dedicated to the deified Hadrian by Antoninus Pius in 145 CE. Some of the temple's substantial remains were incorporated into a 17th-century building designed by architect Carlo Fontana in Rome's Piazza di Pietra.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/666765291> .

