<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/66782793%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Hiera Orgas";
    rdfs:comment "The Hiera Orgas or ‘sacred meadow’ was a tract of land sacred to Demeter and Persephone. It featured in at least two conflicts between Athens and Megara. It was likely located to the north of the Iapis River on the Megarian side of the Athens-Megara border.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/66782793> .

