<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/676120270%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Altar of the Twelve Gods";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/807514119%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A rectangular peribolos with an altar in the centre, built in 522/1 BC, destroyed in the Persian Sack of 480/79 BC, and rebuilt in the late 5th century BC. It was the central milestone from which distances in Attica were measured. The remains are now mostly underneath the Athens-Piraeus Electric Railway.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/676120270> .

