<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/67912717%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "House of the Skeleton";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432873%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called \"The House of the Skeleton\" at Herculaneum is a Roman domus that owes its name to the discovery of a human skeleton during excavations. Carlo Bonucci initially explored it between 1830 and 1831. Amedeo Maiuri completed the excavation in 1927.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/67912717> .

