<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/682032457%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Kar-Mullissu";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/29492%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Kar-Mullissu (Akkadian \"Quay of the goddess Mullissu\") is an Assyrian town in northern Iraq. Modern Karemles (also Karemlash and Karemlish) is located less than twenty-nine km southeast of Mosul (ancient Nineveh). Inscribed bricks of the seventh-century-BCE Assyrian king Sargon II have been discovered there.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/682032457> .

