<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/683591498%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Temple of Amada";
    rdfs:comment "The Temple of Amada is the oldest Egyptian temple known in Nubia. Founded by Pharaoh Thutmose III (18th dynasty), the temple was dedicated to Amun and Re-Horakhty. The decorative program is attributed to Amenhotep II, his son and successor. The temple was relocated to its current position in 1964 along with the Temple of Derr.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/683591498> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/683591498/osm-location-of-temple-of-amada> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
