    rdfs:comment "The tomb of Publius Aelius Callistion, a freedman (libertus) of the emperor Hadrian, is colloquially known as the \"Sedia del Diavolo\". It is located in a piazza that derives its name from the tomb's occupant (piazza Elio Callistio) in Rome's Trieste neighborhood.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/684741498> .

