<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/687988%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Nessana";
    rdfs:comment "Nessana is an ancient site located in the Negev Desert. Established during the Hellenistic period, Nessana has numerous occupational phases including as the site of a Roman military garrison in the fourth century CE. The site flourishes in connection with the Christian pilgrimage route linking the Holy Land to Mount Sinai (sixth and seventh centuries CE).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/687988> .

