<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/68976935%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Monte Sant’Angelo (Tarracina)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/867719962%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A hill at Tarracina where, in Roman times, the sanctuary complex of Jupiter Anxur was built. In the medieval period, it was occupied by a monastery. Secondary deposits displaced by Roman and medieval construction indicate that Monte Sant’Angelo was the site of significant human activity from prehistory through at least the 5th century BCE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/68976935> .

