<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/690025800%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Banāt al-Hassan";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/180784164%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/3601983%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912818%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/924184480%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A multi-period group of mounds in central Mesopotamia (modern Al-Warka District of Iraq), by which passes the modern Basra-Baghdad highway (national highway 1). The site lies about 15 kilometers to the north of the modern town of Al-Warka and about 25 kilometers north-northwest of the ancient site of Uruk. It is not to be confused with Banat al-Hassan in Anbar province, northwest of Baghdad.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/690025800> .

