<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/696289200%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Assur Archive 38";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893945%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "In the street from the Tabira gate into the city (bE7I), excavators found a stone with inscription and small archive of 11 clay tablets in a secondary context. The archive may have belonged to a nearby house. Two tablets are dated to 686 B.C, and another is dated to 675 BC. The archive contains documents such as loans, a purchase document, a document concerning the dissolution of a marriage, as well as an adoption document.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/696289200> .

