        "vici.org 11876: Tramatza, Ponte Romano";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The remains of a Roman bridge at Tramatza cross the Riu di Mare Foghe. Gosner and Nowlin assert that this bridge likely dates to the first century BCE and that its construction may have allowed for better access to the Sardinian interior in the direction of Forum Traiani (Fordongianus). The bridge was repaired in the Middle Ages and again in 1826.";
