<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/631720472> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/vocab#Place>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Gosselin 2023 ",
        "Long 2011 ",
        "Long 2021 (Camargue) ",
        "Long 2021 (Commercio) ";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:description "A Roman commercial port near the modern French town of Saintes-Maries-de-la-Mer is attested by over forty Roman-era shipwrecks discovered in the area since the 1990s, most carrying cargoes of metal. The excavators posit in Roman times a significantly different coastline (generally further south) and an old mouth of the Rhone (Ancien Rhône de Saint-Ferréol), located to the east of Saintes-Maries-de-la-Mer (Long 2011, Figure 1).";
    dcterms:modified "2023-08-16T22:22:36-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Saintes-Marie-de-la-Mer Roman Port";
