    dcterms:description "Ruins of the walled acropolis of ancient Isinda in Lycia are variously said by modern scholars to be located either \"above\" or 2-3km south of the modern Turkish village of Belenli, which is in Antalya province. BAtlas and OpenStreetMap generally agree (within their accuracy and precision limits) with the location further south.";
