    rdfs:label "Grandford";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/649485970%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The remains of a Romano-British settlement at Grandford, Cambridgeshire, were identified by aerial photography. The site lies northwest of the modern town of March and likely lay along the Roman road conventionally known as the Fen Causeway that began at the Roman fort of Longthorpe. The site's extent may have been on the order of 40 acres.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/65728677> .

