    rdfs:label "el-Bara";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/637058243%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "el-Bara (also Bara or al-Bara (Arabic: بارة)) is numbered among one of the so-called \"Dead Cities\" of northwestern Syria. The settlement originates in the fourth century CE and flourishes during the fifth and sixth centuries. It benefited from a favorable position along the route between Antioch and Apamea.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/668207> .

