        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jnovotny>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/rrattenborg>;
    dcterms:description "Kar-Mullissu (Akkadian \"Quay of the goddess Mullissu\") is an Assyrian town in northern Iraq. Modern Karemles (also Karemlash and Karemlish) is located less than twenty-nine km southeast of Mosul (ancient Nineveh). Inscribed bricks of the seventh-century-BCE Assyrian king Sargon II have been discovered there.";
    dcterms:modified "2025-08-01T08:51:46-04:00";
