<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/68843864%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Lycian League";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/638965%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Perhaps formed to protest the annexation of Lycia by Rhodes, by 168–7 BCE the league appears to have gained quasi-autonomy under the domination of Rome. Although the league was a party to a treaty with Iulius Caesar in 46 BCE, by 43 CE the region was annexed by Claudius into the province of Lycia; the league survived and had authority over some local customs and legal matters.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/68843864> .

