        "Pedersén 1998 141";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/ptushingham>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/tseidler>;
    dcterms:description "In the street from the Tabira gate into the city (bE7I), excavators found a stone with inscription and small archive of 11 clay tablets in a secondary context. The archive may have belonged to a nearby house. Two tablets are dated to 686 B.C, and another is dated to 675 BC. The archive contains documents such as loans, a purchase document, a document concerning the dissolution of a marriage, as well as an adoption document.";
