<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/699978029%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Enunmah";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/633091640%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893951%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The temple of the god Nusku, Enunmah (“House of the Exalted Prince”), was located in the Bāb-Lugalerra district of Babylon, in the western half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was one of three temples in that part of Babylon.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/699978029> .

