        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/687852%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Ashqelon/Ascalon was an ancient city in coastal Palestine, located midway between Azotus and Gaza. It became independent in 104 B.C. and remained the only free city in Palestine. Strabo refers to it, while Pliny calls it a free city (oppidum libera).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/687839> .

