<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/605795336%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ušnanis";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/257997170%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648670%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648792%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/652445664%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/907036116%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/930131678%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/944349915%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Ušnanis is a Quean fortress located on the Cilician plain. In the eighth century BC, perhaps only for a short time, Phrygia controlled the territory in which Ušnanis was located. The Assyrian king Sargon II (r. 721-705), after his armies defeated the Phrygian king Midas (= Mitâ of Musku), restored Ušnanis to Que, which was then a province of the Assyrian Empire.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/605795336> .

