<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648555%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Mersin-Yumuktepe";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648789%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/652350%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/652445664%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/911351382%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/944349914%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/944349915%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A tell known today as \"Yumuktepe\" is located at modern Mersin in Turkey. Excavations there, beginning in the 20th century, have provided evidence for continuous and/or successive human settlement beginning in the Neolithic period. Scholars believe that the names \"Ingirâ\" (found in Akkadian sources) and \"Anchiale(ia)\" (found in Greco-Roman sources) are to be associated with the site.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648555> .

